The treatment for classical galactosuria is **lifelong dietary restriction of galactose**. This is because galactose cannot be properly metabolized due to the deficiency of the enzyme galactose dehydrogenase, leading to toxic accumulation of galactose and its metabolites. The goal of treatment is to prevent complications and ensure long-term health.
