<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The change in entropy for the reaction is calculated as:
\[
\Delta G = \Delta H - T\Delta S
\]
Substituting the given molecular entropies:
\[
\Delta S = \sum_{ \text{products}} \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum{ \text{Reactants}} \Delta S_{\text{Reactants}}
\]
Substituting the given molecular entropies:
\[
\Delta S = (2 \times 66.5 + 2 \times 248.2) - (2 \times 91.2 + 3 \times 205.1)
\]
\[
\Delta S = (122 + 490.4) - (182.4 + 510.3)
\]
\[
\Delta S = 512.4 - 692.7 = -180.3 \, \text{J/K mol}
\]

Thus, the change in entropy for the reaction is \(\boxed{-180.3 \, \text{J/K mol}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

