","To determine the geometric mean of the soil-to polished rice transfer factor (TF) for \(^{113}\text{Cs}\), we need to follow these steps:

### Step 1: Understand the Concept
The transfer factor (TF) is the ratio of the concentration of a radionuclide in a crop (e.g., polished rice) to the concentration in the soil.
\[
\text{TF} = \frac{\text{Concentration in Rice}}{\text{Concentration in Soil}}
\]
The geometric mean is calculated by taking the geometric mean of the TF values.

### Step 2: Calculate the Geometric Mean
The geometric mean is calculated as:
\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = \sqrt{\sqrt{\text{TF}_1 \times \text{TF}_2 \times \text{TF}_3 \times \text{TF}_n}}
\]
where \( \text{TF}_1, \text{TF}_2}, \text{TF}_3}, \text{TF}_n \) are the transfer factors.

