\]
Thus, the transfer factor is:
\[
\text{TF} = ({{0.01 \text{ Bq/g/Bkg/kg}}\text{TF}} = 0.01 \text{ Bq/g/Bq/kg}
\]

### Step 4: Calculate the Geometric Mean
Since the transfer factor is constant, the geometric mean is the same as the arithmetic mean, which is the same as the transfer factor itself.
\[
\text{Geometric Mean} = 0.01 \text{ Bq/g/Bq/kg}
\]

