The lumped heat transfer equation is:  
\[
\tau t = \frac{1}{h \rho \rho__ o} \ln \frac{T_0 -T_0_0}{T -T_0}
\]  
where:  
- \(\tau\) is the time constant (\({ \frac{1}{h \rho \rho_ o}} \))  
- \( t \) is the time  
- \( h \) is the convective heat transfer coefficient  
- \( \rho \) is the density  
- \( \rho_ o \) is the density  
- \( T_0 \) is the ambient temperature  
- \( T_0( 0 \) is the initial temperature  
- \( T \) is the temperature at time \( t \)  

