A particle of mass 30 kg is subjected to a force of 32 N. Calculate the acceleration of the particle.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the acceleration of the particle, we use the formula:  
\[
\text{Acceleration} = \frac{\text{Force}}{\text{Mass}}
\]  
Given:  
Mass (m) = 30 kg  
Force (F) = 32 N  
Acceleration (v) = ?  
Substituting the given values into the formula:  
\[
\text{Acceleration} = \frac{32 \text{ N}}{30 \text{ kg}} = 1.033 \text{ m/s}^2
\]  
The acceleration of the particle is \(\boxed{1.033 \text{ m/s}^2}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

